<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Iuvavum</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Iuvavum was a Roman town in the province of Noricum on the Salzach, on the site of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salzburg">Salzburg</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>. Raised to a municipium under Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/claudius">Claudius</a>, it declined in the 5th century, and around 696 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rupert-of-salzburg">Saint Rupert</a> founded a church and monastery among its ruins, the origin of Salzburg.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/iuvavum.jpg" alt="Iuvavum" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jorge Franganillo · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Salzburg_(48489551981).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
